section: profiles
title: Profiles and packs
about: |
  The profiles of the entity: their order, their versions, their templates, and their variables.
rules:
- id: macro-flag-scope
  title: The content of a profile reads no macro
  engines:
  - all
  tier: static
  severity: note
  status: source
  when: (.profiles | length) > 0
  what: |
    A macro is a name and a value, with no version and no digest. A profile whose values or
    manifests read `{{.spectro.macro.<name>}}` gets a new value at once, in the running cluster.
    No publish, no notification, and no audit entry comes with it. The `immutable-clusterprofiles`
    flag of the provider covers the profile, not the macro. This note names each pack that reads
    a macro.
  check:
    kind: static
    expr: |
      [ .profiles[] | .source.name as $p | .packs[]
        | select((((.values // "") + "\n" + ((.manifests // []) | map(.content // "") | join("\n")))) | test("\\{\\{\\s*\\.spectro\\.macro\\."))
        | "profile \($p): pack \(.name)@\(.version) reads a user macro; a change of the macro value changes the cluster with no publish and no audit entry" ]
  reproduce:
  - strata snapshot cluster:<uid> --macros
  evidence:
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.spectrocloud.com/clusters/cluster-management/macros/
  - kind: source
    note: the immutable-clusterprofiles feature_preview flag checks the profile resource alone
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/eks/macro-values.json
    clean: fixtures/eks/addon-profile.json
- id: version-string
  title: Each profile version is MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH
  engines:
  - all
  tier: static
  severity: warn
  status: seen
  when: (.profiles | length) > 0
  what: |
    Palette keeps a version string as given (`1.2`, `v1.2.3`), where its documentation says it
    normalizes it. Two spellings of one version are two versions.
  check:
    kind: static
    expr: |
      [ .profiles[] | select((.source.version // "") | test("^[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+$") | not)
        | "profile \(.source.name) has the version \(.source.version), not MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH" ]
  evidence:
  - kind: run
    ref: '#81'
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/eks/version-v.json
    clean: fixtures/eks/clean.json
- id: variables-in-use
  title: The variable definitions of a version in use stay as they are
  engines:
  - all
  tier: palette
  severity: note
  status: source
  when: (.entity.spec.profiles | length) > 0
  what: |
    Palette refuses a change of the variable definitions of a profile version that a cluster
    uses. Its message: "you must create a new version of your cluster profile before you can
    modify the variables". The packs, the values, and the manifests have no such rule. This note
    names the clusters that use the first profile of the entity, from `status.inUseClusters`.
  check:
    kind: palette
    method: GET
    path: /v1/clusterprofiles/{{ .entity.spec.profiles[0].uid }}
    expr: |
      .entity.spec.profiles[0].uid as $u
      | if (.response.ok | not) then ["Palette cannot read profile \($u): \(.response.body.code // .response.status)"]
        elif ((.response.body.status.inUseClusters // []) | length) > 0
        then ["profile \(.response.body.metadata.name // $u) is in use by \(.response.body.status.inUseClusters | length | count_of("cluster")) (\([ .response.body.status.inUseClusters[] | .name // .uid ] | join(", "))): a change of its variable definitions is refused; make a new version"]
        else [] end
  reproduce:
  - '{{ palette_curl }} "${PALETTE_API:-https://api.spectrocloud.com}/v1/clusterprofiles/{{ .entity.spec.profiles[0].uid }}" | jq ''.status.inUseClusters'''
  evidence:
  - kind: source
    note: Palette tests the clusters that use the profile version before it updates the variables
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.spectrocloud.com/profiles/cluster-profiles/create-cluster-profiles/define-profile-variables/modify-cluster-profile-variables/
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/eks/profile-in-use.json
    clean: fixtures/eks/full-records.json
